1. EC2 Setup Instructions

    Step 1: Launch EC2 Instances
            Launch 5 t2.medium instances (Ubuntu 22.04) using AWS Academy, 1 master and 4 workers
            Open ports 22 (SSH) and 7077, 8080 (Spark)

    Step 2: Install Java and Spark
            sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y openjdk-17-jdk wget
            wget https://downloads.apache.org/spark/spark-3.4.1/spark-3.4.1-bin-hadoop3.tgz

            Set environment variables in ~/.bashrc.

    Step 3: Configure Spark Standalone Cluster
            On master: ./sbin/start-master.sh
            On each worker: ./sbin/start-slave.sh spark://<master-private-ip>:7077

2. Model Training Using Spark

      Run the following command on the master node:
      spark-submit \
      --class com.cs643.assignment2.App \
      --master spark://<master-private-ip>:7077 \
      --packages org.apache.hadoop:hadoop-aws:3.3.1,com.amazonaws:aws-java-sdk-bundle:1.11.901 \
      target/wine-predictor-1.0.jar \
      s3a://cs643-wine-date-pn338/TrainingDataset.csv \
      s3a://cs643-wine-date-pn338/ValidationDataset.csv

      This trains logistic regression and random forest classifiers.
      The best model (Random Forest) is saved to:s3a://cs643-wine-date-pn338/best_model/
3. Running Prediction in Docker

    Step 1: Build Docker Image
            Create Dockerfile:
            FROM openjdk:17-jdk-slim
            COPY target/wine-predictor-1.0.jar /app/wine-predictor.jar
            ENTRYPOINT ["java", "-cp", "/app/wine-predictor.jar", "com.cs643.assignment2.Test"]
      Build and push:
            docker build -t <your-dockerhub-username>/wine-predictor .
            docker push <your-dockerhub-username>/wine-predictor
    Step 2: Run Docker Container
            docker run \
            -v ~/.aws:/root/.aws \
            <your-dockerhub-username>/wine-predictor \
            s3a://cs643-wine-date-pn338/best_model \
            s3a://cs643-wine-date-pn338/ValidationDataset.csv
    This will output predictions and the model's F1 score.

4. Output 
    Model Performance - F1 Score: 0.5539

5. Note 
        Ensure your EC2 instance has an IAM role with S3 access or configure credentials in ~/.aws/credentials.
        If using private buckets, ensure permissions are correctly set.
